{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"agatoid-relatable-phoebe","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nClosing REB-3115 S3 T3 (`67d4-ecba-cf95-4353`) FAULTED the completion-verification close gate: the verifier's agentic evidence-search loop repeated an identical `read_file` call and was force-aborted by the in-flight runaway guard, TRUNCATING the evidence search. The truncated run then reported a **FAIL / \"3 unmet criteria; not closing\"** in which 2 of 3 findings self-flag as *\"This is an evidence gap, not a demonstrated failure of the work.\"* — i.e. the gate produced a blocking verdict from its own execution failure, not from a real AC miss. Neither PASS nor a legitimate FAIL/BLOCK → a fault in the gate itself.\n\n## Observed verbatim\n```\nWARNING rebar.llm.run_failure: llm call [completion-verifier] mode=agentic model=bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 aborted a runaway tool-call loop in 201.0s requests=56 tool_calls=63 distinct=37 max_consecutive_repeat=24 distinct_ratio_window=0.042 top_repeats=[{'signature': 'read_file:168d61f3', 'count': 24}, {'signature': 'read_file:b749c833', 'count': 4}]\nError: completion verification FAILED for 67d4-ecba-cf95-4353 — 3 unmet criteria; not closing.\n  - Venue-gated Cloud/DC verified fakes pass before the coordinator default changes.: No venue-gating or Cloud/DC verified-fake tests were found ...\n  - Migrated families route failure fusing through the new endpoint-failure scoped fuse; legacy ad-hoc retry nesting is unreachable ...: The bounded evidence search was exhausted (three unique evidence responses) ... This is an evidence gap, not a demonstrated failure of the work.\n  - Historical replay of the completed 1,200-run slice shows zero premature stop ...: The bounded evidence search was exhausted (three unique evidence responses) ... This is an evidence gap, not a demonstrated failure of the work.\n```\n\n## Impact\nBlocks a CERTIFIED (no-force) close of merged work (change 2218, sha d49466b5e960). AC5/AC6 tests demonstrably landed (test_guarded_execute_wiring_adds_no_legacy_retry_nesting; rp03 replay in test_scoped_pass_fuse.py) but were unreached because the loop aborted. AC2 (\"venue-gated Cloud/DC verified fakes\") may be a genuine content gap — to be assessed separately.\n\n## Step 0 orientation\n- 0(a): Chronic area. Related CLOSED prior art: epic `10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b` (rework completion-verifier context mgmt: batched AC verification, context ceilings, pre-loading — \"runaway duplicate tool-call loops, one run repeated an identical search_files call 144x\"); bug `46a2-9c1a-d855-4706` (verifier burns step budget re-issuing one identical tool call → adopted typed RunawayToolLoopError → per-criterion bounded recovery + tool-free finalization); bug `70bc-ab05-6d4c-45a0` (max_consecutive_repeat blind to cycles); story `561e-e186-a902-461c` (force-with-reason bypass used when bounded recovery aborted a runaway loop). This is a REGRESSION/recurrence of a fixed class — the recovery+reconcile path did not neutralize the fault into an INDETERMINATE/non-blocking outcome.\n- 0(b): reported on/after d49466b5e960 (current tip; the fault occurred against this build).\n- 0(c): debug worktree CURRENT at d49466b5e960 (= origin/main).\n\n## Suspected seams (leads to test, not conclusions)\n- `src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py`: repetition summary + in-flight runaway guard (window_distinct_ratio, max_consecutive_repeat, REPETITION_WINDOW thresholds).\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`: agent loop, runaway abort, bounded evidence text handling, finalize_outcome.\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py`: `_all_insufficiency` (:118) reads framework-set `evidence_sufficient: false` markers to distinguish insufficiency from genuine unmet — a mixed set (>=1 possibly-genuine unmet + evidence-gap records) may NOT classify as all-insufficiency, so the whole FAIL blocks.\n- `src/rebar/llm/completion.py`: step-budget clamp (steps_per_criterion, loop limits).\n\n## Two open questions for RCA\n1. WHY did the agentic evidence loop repeat an identical `read_file` 24x (what makes it loop rather than progress)?\n2. WHY was the resulting truncated/evidence-gap outcome reported as a blocking FAIL rather than a non-blocking INDETERMINATE fault (i.e. did insufficiency-reconciliation fail to fire, or get poisoned by one mixed finding)?\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Proven root cause of the runaway-loop fault + the blocking-FAIL classification, confirmed by a discriminating experiment with a runtime oracle, rivals ruled out, naming changeable artifact(s).\n- [ ] A RED→GREEN regression test (held out from the fixer) that reproduces the fault and returns to RED under a defect-seeded mutation.\n- [ ] Fix lands through Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1), applier of the fix is restoration not creation, no test weakened.\n- [ ] Defect attributed via `--caused-by` (or explicit unattributable finding) with RCA comment.","id":"2dcb-5468-b734-4b60","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion-verifier close gate FAULTs: runaway read_file loop aborts evidence search, then reports the truncation as a blocking FAIL (3 'evidence gap' unmet criteria)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787670487707752001,"uuid":"aee63d30-6cfd-4ae5-98d7-c0cd9a9492cf"}